{"message":"For minimizing ATM costs abroad, the best option is generally the World Blue Account: Rho charges $0 for foreign ATM withdrawals and automatically rebates foreign ATM-operator fees up to $100 per calendar month. However, it has a $50 monthly maintenance fee and requires maintaining at least $10,000; it is listed as a business checking account.

The Bluest Account also charges $0 for foreign ATM withdrawals and rebates third-party ATM fees up to $50 per month, but it requires a $75,000 opening deposit, a $112,500 daily balance to avoid its $75 monthly fee, and may not be practical for a three-month trip.

For either account, foreign ATM operators may charge fees beyond the monthly rebate cap. When withdrawing, choose checking and local-currency billing rather than dynamic currency conversion. Are you looking for a personal or business checking account, and do you expect to maintain the required balance?"}
